---
interface Props {
	/** Mention the reviewer's verdicts as the one human-judged element. */
	humanContent?: boolean;
}
const { humanContent = true } = Astro.props;
---

<aside role="note" class="rounded-xl border border-rule-strong bg-accent-soft px-4 py-3 text-xs leading-relaxed text-ink-2 sm:text-sm">
	<p>
		<strong class="text-ink">AI-generated and unverified.</strong>{" "}
		The audit findings and the pass/fail grades here come from AI models: the findings are two AI auditors' judgments and the grades are the benchmark's native AI judges, so any of them can be wrong.
		{humanContent && <>{" "}The only human judgments are <strong class="text-ink">the reviewer's own verdicts</strong> on the 25 hand-audited criteria, labeled as such.{" "}</>}
		Task instructions and rubric text are Harvey's, reproduced under its MIT license.
	</p>
</aside>
